{"author":{"id":"b28ace64b4a52eef863f0423a2df7021241dd0c0bac0a20931e2333fd3a1b77e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794738473,"nonce":"DHi8Nec+VC8aulgL8ltcqUIAtpM=","title":"Issues dialog: \"+ New Issue\" button is white-on-white in the dark (\"black\") theme","message":"## Symptom (reported by user, black/dark theme)\n\nOpening the Issues dialog (`sidebar.footer.action` → git-bug overlay), the primary **\"+ New Issue\"** button in the list toolbar renders with a whitish background. Its label is white, so the text is unreadable. Only on hover does the background change and the label become readable.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`src/client/factory.js` — `STYLE_ID` CSS block:\n\n```css\n.gb-btn-primary{background:var(--dsw-alias-brand-primary,#4a6cf7);border-color:transparent;color:#fff}\n```\n\n- In the dark palette `--dsw-alias-brand-primary` resolves to `--dsw-static-neutral-bluish-50` = `rgb(249,250,251)` — a *near-white* fill (see `packages/client/ui-theme/src/styles/design-platform.css`, dark block). The hardcoded `color:#fff` then paints white on near-white.\n- On hover `.gb-btn:hover:not(:disabled)` (specificity 0,3,0) beats `.gb-btn-primary` (0,1,0) and swaps the fill to `--dsw-alias-fill-l1` (translucent white over the dark panel), so the white label suddenly reads — exactly the reported behaviour.\n- With the fallback `#4a6cf7` (when the token is missing) the button is fine, which is why it only shows in themes that define `brand-primary` as a light accent.\n\n## Fix proposal\n\nUse the theme's paired primary-button tokens, the same way DSH's own `ui-primitives` Button module does (`Button.module.css`):\n\n```css\n.gb-btn-primary{\n  background:var(--dsw-alias-button-primary-fill,#4a6cf7);\n  border-color:transparent;\n  color:var(--dsw-alias-label-primary-foreground,#fff);\n}\n.gb-btn-primary:hover:not(:disabled){background:var(--dsw-alias-button-primary-hover,#3a5be0)}\n```\n\n`--dsw-alias-label-primary-foreground` is `bluish-1000` (`rgb(15,17,21)`) in dark and `bluish-00` in light, so the label tracks the fill in every palette. The dedicated `:hover` rule also stops the generic `.gb-btn` hover from overriding the primary fill.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- In dark/black theme (and any custom theme defining `brand-primary`), \"+ New Issue\" shows readable text (no white-on-white).\n- Hover keeps a deliberate primary-hover fill instead of falling back to the generic translucent fill.\n- Light theme unchanged: dark fill + light label.\n- `npm run build` regenerates `lib/client.js` (source and bundle currently carry the buggy rule verbatim).\n\nTouch points: `src/client/factory.js` (CSS + `gb-btn-primary` rule), rebuilt `lib/client.js`.","files":null}]}